# RentEase — shared development environment reference
#
# This monorepo uses per-service .env files, not a single root .env.
# Copy each service's .env.sample to .env in its directory, or run:
#   bash scripts/setup-cloud-env.sh
#
# Shared secrets (must be identical across all backend services):
#   JWT_SECRET       — JWT signing key
#   SERVICE_SECRET   — inter-service auth (identity ↔ organization)
#
# Identity-service only:
#   ENCRYPTION_KEY   — exactly 32 characters, for PII encryption at rest
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET — optional, for Google OAuth
#
# Per-service .env templates:
#   apps/identity-service/.env.sample
#   apps/organization-service/.env.sample
#   apps/property-service/.env.sample
#   apps/billing-service/.env.sample
#
# Frontend:
#   apps/web/.env.local  →  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
